### What are the core entities?

The core entities are `User`, `Product`, `Cart`, `CartItem`, `DiscountStrategy`, and `CheckoutService`.

```java
package com.bank.cart.model;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class Product {
    private final String productId;
    private final String name;
    private final BigDecimal price;
    private int stock;

    public Product(String productId, String name,
                   BigDecimal price, int stock) {
        this.productId = productId;
        this.name = name;
        this.price = price;
        this.stock = stock;
    }

    public synchronized boolean decrementStock(int quantity) {
        if (stock < quantity) return false;
        stock -= quantity;
        return true;
    }

    public String getProductId() { return productId; }
    public String getName() { return name; }
    public BigDecimal getPrice() { return price; }
    public int getStock() { return stock; }
}
```

```java
package com.bank.cart.model;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class CartItem {
    private final Product product;
    private int quantity;

    public CartItem(Product product, int quantity) {
        this.product = product;
        this.quantity = quantity;
    }

    public BigDecimal getLineTotal() {
        return product.getPrice().multiply(
                BigDecimal.valueOf(quantity));
    }

    public Product getProduct() { return product; }
    public int getQuantity() { return quantity; }
    public void setQuantity(int quantity) {
        this.quantity = quantity;
    }
}
```

### How does the Cart work?

A Cart holds items and computes a running subtotal.

```java
package com.bank.cart.model;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.*;

public class Cart {
    private final String userId;
    private final Map<String, CartItem> items;

    public Cart(String userId) {
        this.userId = userId;
        this.items = new LinkedHashMap<>();
    }

    public void addItem(Product product, int quantity) {
        items.merge(product.getProductId(),
                new CartItem(product, quantity),
                (existing, newItem) -> {
                    existing.setQuantity(
                            existing.getQuantity() + quantity);
                    return existing;
                });
        System.out.println("Added " + quantity + " x "
                + product.getName() + " to cart");
    }

    public void removeItem(String productId) {
        items.remove(productId);
    }

    public BigDecimal getSubtotal() {
        return items.values().stream()
                .map(CartItem::getLineTotal)
                .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);
    }

    public Collection<CartItem> getItems() {
        return items.values();
    }

    public boolean isEmpty() { return items.isEmpty(); }
}
```

### How does the DiscountStrategy work?

Discounts are pulled into a strategy interface so marketing can launch new promotions without touching checkout code.

```java
package com.bank.cart.service;

import com.bank.cart.model.Cart;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public interface DiscountStrategy {
    BigDecimal applyDiscount(Cart cart, BigDecimal subtotal);
}
```

```java
package com.bank.cart.service;

import com.bank.cart.model.Cart;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.math.RoundingMode;

public class PercentageDiscount implements DiscountStrategy {
    private final BigDecimal percentage;

    public PercentageDiscount(BigDecimal percentage) {
        this.percentage = percentage;
    }

    @Override
    public BigDecimal applyDiscount(Cart cart, BigDecimal subtotal) {
        BigDecimal discount = subtotal.multiply(percentage)
                .divide(new BigDecimal("100"), 2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);
        System.out.println("Applied " + percentage + "% discount: -"
                + discount);
        return subtotal.subtract(discount);
    }
}
```

```java
package com.bank.cart.service;

import com.bank.cart.model.Cart;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class FlatDiscount implements DiscountStrategy {
    private final BigDecimal flatAmount;

    public FlatDiscount(BigDecimal flatAmount) {
        this.flatAmount = flatAmount;
    }

    @Override
    public BigDecimal applyDiscount(Cart cart, BigDecimal subtotal) {
        BigDecimal discounted = subtotal.subtract(flatAmount);
        if (discounted.compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) < 0) {
            discounted = BigDecimal.ZERO;
        }
        System.out.println("Applied flat discount: -" + flatAmount);
        return discounted;
    }
}
```

### How does the checkout flow work?

Checkout is the critical, must-be-atomic flow. It validates inventory, applies discounts, charges payment, and decrements stock.

```java
package com.bank.cart.service;

import com.bank.cart.model.*;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

public class CheckoutService {
    private final PaymentStrategy paymentStrategy;
    private final DiscountStrategy discountStrategy;

    public CheckoutService(PaymentStrategy paymentStrategy,
                            DiscountStrategy discountStrategy) {
        this.paymentStrategy = paymentStrategy;
        this.discountStrategy = discountStrategy;
    }

    public BigDecimal checkout(Cart cart, String userId) {
        if (cart.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Cart is empty");
        }

        // Step 1: Validate inventory
        for (CartItem item : cart.getItems()) {
            if (item.getProduct().getStock() < item.getQuantity()) {
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Insufficient stock for "
                        + item.getProduct().getName());
            }
        }

        // Step 2: Apply discounts
        BigDecimal subtotal = cart.getSubtotal();
        BigDecimal total = discountStrategy.applyDiscount(
                cart, subtotal);

        // Step 3: Charge payment
        boolean paid = paymentStrategy.charge(userId, total);
        if (!paid) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Payment failed");
        }

        // Step 4: Decrement stock (only after payment succeeds)
        for (CartItem item : cart.getItems()) {
            if (!item.getProduct().decrementStock(
                    item.getQuantity())) {
                // Refund and abort
                paymentStrategy.refund(userId, total);
                throw new IllegalStateException(
                        "Stock changed during checkout for "
                        + item.getProduct().getName());
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Checkout complete for " + userId
                + ", total: " + total);
        return total;
    }
}
```

